# =============================================================================
# Suricata threshold.config — Adversary-in-a-Box Lab
#
# G5.5 (Gap K): an operator-tunable layer of alert-volume control, loaded
# via `threshold-file` in suricata.yaml, for sids whose own rule in
# local.rules carries no inline threshold/flow-rate limit. An entry here
# for a sid that ALREADY has an inline `threshold:` REPLACES that rule's
# threshold rather than adding a second layer on top of it (confirmed
# empirically: pairing a `type limit, count 1` entry here with sid:1000041's
# inline `type both, count 5` made it fire on the very first matching
# packet instead of waiting for a burst) -- so this file is reserved for
# sids without their own inline threshold, not a way to further tune ones
# that already have one.
#
# Syntax: threshold gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>, type <limit|threshold|both>,
#         track <by_src|by_dst>, count <N>, seconds <N>
# gen_id 1 is the standard signature generator (all local.rules alerts).
# =============================================================================

# sid:1000040/1000043 (SMB1/SMB2 pass-the-hash) match on the SMB header
# magic at the start of a TCP segment with no threshold of their own --
# a single active SMB session sends many PDUs, each a fresh segment
# starting with that magic, so the rule as written can alert once per PDU.
# Collapse repeated hits from the same source into one alert per minute.
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 1000040, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 60
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 1000043, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 60
